      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Im on board with the feeling this was rushed too. There's a lot of weird decisions that feel like they completely overlooked VR users entirely. Just basic \"you can move it around! Look!\" But thats it. Typing on this keyboard has been more of a pain. \n\nI actually thought about using my keyboard wirelessly for the first time in years after this dropped. Might just do that.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-09-12T18:49:48.716Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Simply put, the new keyboard layout right now sucks.\n\nSeriously.. two button presses to access most keys and it feels crammed when typing, For mobile platforms it's fine, not for us VR players.\n\nMy suggestion is a setting that **REVITALIZES** the old keyboard layout.\n\nYes, the keyword is ***revitalize***, Make the new keyboard's layout match almost EXACTLY to the old one as a setting, showed on the first two pictures.\n\nBecause in my experience, it's a hell lot more accessible that way, and also, i don't want to press two separate buttons to access most keys, this and the crammed feeling can impact how fast you can type in VR.\n\nAnother thing that I'm very negative about is that the input field UI (from what i heard) cannot be moved around BY DESIGN, which contributes to the unnatural positioning of this new keyboard and it strains my wrists over-time.\n\n- speaking of such, maybe merge that input window with this new keyboard if possible.\n\nlastly, this whole thing feels rushed.",
